  Section 4: banding: 
  - Each band: seeds gated by bin core (L101), extension unbounded in m/z, own visited (L52).
  - Failure modes: (i) same feature straddling boundary gets traced independently in both bands → duplicate traces with identical/overlapping members — impossible in OpenMS (global visited); (ii) OpenMS's kill mechanism (closest peak visited → missed → eventual termination) doesn't fire across bands → traces OpenMS would have terminated early run to completion → extra/longer traces; (iii) conversely, cross-band contention resolution is nondeterministic if bands run concurrently (output order), though per-band deterministic; (iv) boundary in raw bins with per-frame calibration drift → core boundary wobbles in m/z; a feature's peaks in different frames classify differently, but only the seed's bin matters.
  - Bounded: duplication limited to features whose ±3σ span crosses a boundary — O(#boundaries × σ/ band width) fraction; each straddler at most (#bands it touches) copies. Never subtractive → cannot explain a peptide deficit; if anything duplicates/inflates, and could perturb FDR/feature-linking downstream.

